{
  "tema": 6672,
  "slug": "numeros-como-pronombres",
  "titulo": "Numbers as pronouns",
  "subtitulo": "¿Cuántos hermanos tienes? —Dos. ¿Quieres un taco? —Dame uno.",
  "foto": "t08.jpg",
  "regla": "A number can stand alone, replacing a noun already mentioned: tengo dos. Alone, one is uno or una (never un), 21 is veintiuno or veintiuna, and hundreds agree too: doscientas.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "When the noun is clear, the number can replace it: **¿Cuántos hermanos tienes? —Tengo dos.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Watch **one**: before a masculine noun it's **un**, but alone it's **uno**. Feminine is always **una**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "",
            "Before a noun",
            "Alone"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "1, masculine",
              "un taco",
              "uno"
            ],
            [
              "1, feminine",
              "una tortilla",
              "una"
            ],
            [
              "21, masculine",
              "veintiún años",
              "veintiuno"
            ],
            [
              "21, feminine",
              "veintiuna personas",
              "veintiuna"
            ],
            [
              "200, feminine",
              "doscientas páginas",
              "doscientas"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Numbers ending in one (31, 41…) and hundreds (200–900) also agree in gender."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With the article, **los dos, las tres** = _both, all three_: **los dos duermen conmigo**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Uno de, dos de** + group = _one of, two of_: **uno de mis amigos**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "¿Cuántos hermanos tienes? —==Dos==.",
              "en": "How many siblings do you have? —Two."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Quieres un taco? —Sí, dame ==uno==.",
              "en": "Do you want a taco? —Yes, give me one."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Cuántas cervezas trajiste? —==Una== nada más.",
              "en": "How many beers did you bring? —Just one."
            },
            {
              "es": "Compré tres tablas, pero ==una== tiene un golpe.",
              "en": "I bought three boards, but one has a ding."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Cuántos alumnos hay en tu clase? —==Veintiuno==.",
              "en": "How many students are in your class? —Twenty-one."
            },
            {
              "es": "Tengo dos perros y ==los dos== duermen conmigo.",
              "en": "I have two dogs and they both sleep with me."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Cuántas páginas leíste? —==Doscientas==.",
              "en": "How many pages did you read? —Two hundred."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Uno de== mis amigos entrena jiu-jitsu.",
              "en": "One of my friends trains jiu-jitsu."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
